// ---- ply's decision points (scripts/decision-points.mjs) ----
// Function globs (`<file>#<fn>:*`) are used where every point of a function has the same space: a new fail() in that
// function is then claimed for the same space, and gate c's claims check fails unless that space's cells reach it.
// The generated block was proposed from a recorded run (the space whose runners reached each site: enumerated first,
// then random, then curated) and reviewed; the manual block above it decides what a run cannot.
const INTERNAL = 'an internal invariant (code internal): true by construction, no input reaches it; a mutation test holds the check in place';
